### 1. Login and save JWT
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

> {% client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken); %}


### 2. Get authenticated user profile
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 3. Update user profile
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jonas",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}


### 4. Get profile after updating
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 5. Change password
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Password123",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword456"
}


### 6. Login with the new password
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "NewPassword456"
}

> {% client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken); %}


### 7. Update with invalid profile data (expect 400)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}


### 8. Change password with incorrect current password (expect 401)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "WrongPassword",
  "newPassword": "AnotherPassword123"
}


### 9. Access profile without JWT (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me


### 10. Access profile with invalid JWT (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token